# Release line that `make latest` / `--latest` must stay within.
#
# Every resource in this catalog imports the Maestro / Skills engine as
# `rasa.calm_v2`, which ships ONLY on the 3.19.0.devN pre-release line.
#
# Verified against PyPI on 2026-08-25 by inspecting the published wheels:
#   3.19.0.dev7  contains rasa/calm_v2/   (2180 files)
#   3.19.1       does NOT                 (1932 files)
#   3.19.0       does NOT
# `calm_v2` is the only package that differs between the two; stable adds no
# renamed replacement, exposes no `calm` extra, and no separate rasa-calm
# distribution exists. So "newest on PyPI" (3.19.1) is a release that cannot
# import a single resource here.
#
# This is no longer enforced by comment alone: `make outdated` probes the
# newest release for the module and `make migrate VERSION=...` refuses a target
# that lacks it. When Maestro reaches the stable line, `make outdated` will say
# so — at that point delete this file and run `make migrate VERSION=<stable>`.
3.19.0.dev
